# Example ReRDMFT input file: water molecule. DEBUG TRUE alone (VERBOSE
# defaults to 0) runs only the cheap DEBUG cross-checks (the O(n^4)
# efficient gradient, the finite-difference test, for NON_REL, C4_DHF,
# AND X2C-HF); add VERBOSE 1 (see water_debug_verbose1.inp) to also run
# the more expensive O(n^5) GeneralizedFock.h dense-2-RDM cross-check,
# or VERBOSE 2 (see water_debug_verbose2.inp) to additionally validate
# the mixed real/imaginary Hessian block. HESSIAN_NON_REL/HESSIAN_4C/
# HESSIAN_X2C are independent of DEBUG/VERBOSE: they build and
# diagonalize the FULL cheap orbital-rotation Hessian to confirm
# NON_REL and X2C-HF are genuine minima (X2C-HF has no negative-energy
# branch to admit a downhill rotation into, unlike C4_DHF) and C4_DHF a
# saddle point.
NELEC 10
BASIS water-sto-3g.gbs
X2C TRUE
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
DEBUG TRUE
HESSIAN_NON_REL TRUE
HESSIAN_4C TRUE
HESSIAN_X2C TRUE

GEOMETRY
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.757000   0.586000
H   0.000000  -0.757000   0.586000
END
